      "writtenOn": "2021-07-26T16:24:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, mutating the builtin symbol tables results in lots of weird problems. Your Program\u0027s pool will go away when the Program dies, and then you have stale pointers inside the built-in symbol table that live on, and crash if you ever access them. If nothing else, they definitely crash once the symbol table is freed (when the compiler goes). So it\u0027s not harmless by any stretch.",
      "parentUuid": "021d9602_5af3675d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "d7a2c0386f2966cb281203b372b2c5afa471c352",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30458b52_6d7ddbf0",
        "filename": "src/sksl/ir/SkSLSymbolTable.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 5640
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-26T17:05:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SymbolTable\u0027s parent is a shared_ptr. The builtin pool can\u0027t go away while there are still programs in memory.",
      "parentUuid": "033e8d01_59d11f80",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "d7a2c0386f2966cb281203b372b2c5afa471c352",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c723766b_7cf68de8",
        "filename": "src/sksl/ir/SkSLSymbolTable.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-26T18:08:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that when a Program disappears, every allocation made by the Program disappears simultaneously as well, because they are all stored in the program\u0027s SkSL::MemoryPool. If the Program\u0027s strings have ended up in a built-in SymbolTable, that SymbolTable will continue to exist past the Program\u0027s lifetime, but the built-in SymbolTable now contains pointers to objects (strings, types) that used to exist in that Program\u0027s SkSL::MemoryPool, and now no longer exist at all. \n\nWe actually detect this issue and report it as a leak when the MemoryPool is destroyed in debug. But in release mode, we don\u0027t leak check, so when the SymbolTable is eventually destroyed, it will crash trying to delete those leaked objects.",
      "parentUuid": "30458b52_6d7ddbf0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "d7a2c0386f2966cb281203b372b2c5afa471c352",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
